- How to handle key compromise—how to revoke and re-key conversations without losing history?

## Implementation
- PHPickerViewController (iOS 14+) via UIViewControllerRepresentable for SwiftUI video capture with 10s limit
- AVAssetImageGenerator extracts thumbnails from captured video
- FileManager.documentDirectory stores app-managed .mov and .png files
- SwiftUI LazyVGrid displays searchable grid with TextField search and DatePicker date filter
- @State manages Codable metadata JSON persistence
- All controls need .accessibilityLabel() for VoiceOver

## Key Code
```swift
struct VideoPicker: UIViewControllerRepresentable {
    @Binding var videoURL: URL?
    func makeUIViewController() -> PHPickerViewController {
        var config = PHPickerConfiguration()
        config.filter = .videos
        config.selectionLimit = 1
        let picker = PHPickerViewController(configuration: config)
        return picker
    }
}

struct CheckpointView: View {
    @State private var videos: [VideoMetadata] = []
    @State private var searchText = ""
    @State private var selectedDate = Date()

    var filteredVideos: [VideoMetadata] {
        videos.filter { video in
            video.title.localizedCaseInsensitiveContains(searchText) &&
            Calendar.current.isDate(video.date, inSameDayAs: selectedDate)
        }
    }

    var body: some View {
        LazyVGrid(columns: [GridItem(.adaptive(minimum: 100))]) {
            ForEach(filteredVideos) { video in
                VideoCell(video: video)
                    .accessibilityLabel("Video \(video.title)")
            }
        }
    }
}
```

